# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# NOTE: NO backticks and NO dollar-sign in the desc/blurb text below (shell-eval fragility -- see CLAUDE.md).
register_gate "tests/test_pause_ack.py" "PAUSE ACK GATE: PASS" "pause-ack tier (the conclusion that actually changes behavior)" "pause-ack (一時停止): a MATERIAL coupling (a REAL in-flight cross-PR collision -- serialize/serialize_soft, or a warn WITH an in-flight partner) posts conclusion action_required until someone EXPLICITLY acknowledges THIS specific coupling via the veripsa-ack label; it is NOT a blunt block (proceed by acknowledging = a conscious RECORDED stop-and-engage, then it clears). STATELESS -- the ack state is the GitHub label + a content-free coupling-snapshot hash embedded in Veripsa's own prior comment (NO DB, NO DDL). Proven on the real render.apply_pause_ack across the full lifecycle: (1) material + no ack -> action_required + the snapshot marker + the proceed-by-ack instruction; (2) + the label with prior-hash == current -> neutral (acknowledged, recorded); (3) the coupling materially changes (different partner/paths -> a different hash) with the label still on -> action_required AGAIN (re-raised) + the stale ack detected and the label slated for removal + a re-acknowledge instruction; (4) a SOLO hotspot/split notice with NO in-flight partner stays neutral (NO false pause -- precision); (5) clear -> success unchanged. Content-free: the snapshot hashes ONLY the change refs + colliding paths/symbols Veripsa already surfaces -- never a file body; the embedded marker carries only the hex digest" "pause-ack tier: material coupling -> action_required until acknowledged (veripsa-ack label + content-free snapshot hash, stateless/no-DB); re-raises on a material change, never false-pauses a solo notice, clear stays success" 30
